    {
      "description": "Bottom line: There is no single \"best\" vector DB — match it to your constraints. Use pgvector if you already run PostgreSQL, Qdrant for strong metadata filtering and a generous free tier under ~50M vectors, Milvus to scale toward billions, Pinecone for zero-ops serverless, and Chroma for local prototyping.\nDeep dive: Vector Database Comparison — a decision framework by scale, deployment, filtering, hybrid search, and cost.",
      "items": [],
      "title": "Vector Databases"
